  "description": "The COUNT SOLO is an affordable cross-country bike that is suitable for everyday use. The lightweight aluminium frame with balanced geometry ensures a harmonious and safe riding experience. High-quality and robust components complete the image of the all-rounder mountain bike. In addition to the classic size recommendations, the five frame sizes also give you the option of selecting the right size for your intended use – if you care about a particularly agile and playful riding feel, this can be achieved with a smaller frame size, while a larger size offers more stable riding behaviour at high speeds. Thanks to Solo-Air suspension, the RockShox Judy Silver TK can be adjusted to your individual needs. With its 100mm travel, it offers convincing suspension performance in a wide range of riding situations – harder tuning offers more control on the trail, softer tuning gives you a comfortable ride in everyday use. The lockout function can be controlled from the handlebar to allow for efficient pedalling and a good uphill performance of the Count Solo. The EAGLE shifting system with components of the SX groupset is the absolute all-round carefree 1x drivetrain by SRAM. It impresses with a high gear range of 500%, smooth gear shifts and absolute reliability. Its simple handling makes it the ideal shifting system for beginners and all those who want to focus on the essentials. With the hydraulic disc brake by SHIMANO, you can control the braking power in every situation. The special design reduces noise during braking and ensures consistent braking performance in a wide range of conditions. In combination with the Kenda Booster tyres, the robust WH-MT500 wheels by Shimano will take you safely over almost every terrain. There are thus no more limits to your spirit of discovery. * approx. 13.9 kg, may vary by up to +/- 5 % due to manufacturing tolerances, weight for matt black grey frame, size M, without pedals",
